WEBVTT

1
00:00:35.336 --> 00:00:37.038
<font color="#D900D9">(FOOTSTEPS RUNNING)</font>

2
00:00:37.138 --> 00:00:39.404
<font color="#D900D9">(MAN BREATHING HEAVILY)</font>

3
00:01:03.864 --> 00:01:06.498
<font color="#D900D9">(PANTING)</font>

4
00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:47.427
You know I can't keep this, right?

5
00:01:51.678 --> 00:01:54.115
Your grandfather made it for you.

6
00:01:54.515 --> 00:01:56.882
To give to the man I love.

7
00:01:59.253 --> 00:02:00.919
Come on, you won't miss me.

8
00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:06.348
Practice at 6:00 every morning. Classes.

9
00:02:06.994 --> 00:02:10.015
All those college guys.

10
00:02:20.374 --> 00:02:24.303
Got to pack. Meeting my parents
for breakfast before I hit the road.

11
00:02:50.397 --> 00:02:52.471
What you got there?

12
00:02:55.476 --> 00:02:58.042
I owe you for the necklace.

13
00:03:07.921 --> 00:03:09.805
You know what it means to me.

14
00:03:21.835 --> 00:03:24.439
- Do you have water?
- I'm gonna hit Roland's on the way out.

15
00:03:24.539 --> 00:03:26.741
I could always just load up a cooler,
make you some sandwiches.

16
00:03:26.841 --> 00:03:29.108
It's not that long of a drive.

17
00:03:34.615 --> 00:03:36.105
Look, you know I...

18
00:03:40.654 --> 00:03:42.621
Give me a safe arrival call, all right?

19
00:03:44.558 --> 00:03:47.426
Better pick up.
Don't want to hear the machine.

20
00:03:52.866 --> 00:03:54.700
<font color="#D900D9">(ENGINE STARTS)</font>

21
00:04:08.982 --> 00:04:11.016
<font color="#D900D9">(PHONE RINGING)</font>

22
00:04:20.627 --> 00:04:22.663
<font color="#D900D9">(MACHINE BEEPS)</font>

23
00:04:22.763 --> 00:04:24.965
<i>Ben, it's Joe.</i>

24
00:04:25.065 --> 00:04:29.269
<i>Got a job here for you this morning.
Guy wants to go out to the reach.</i>

25
00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:31.739
<i>Let me know if you can't
be here in an hour.</i>

26
00:04:31.839 --> 00:04:33.739
<font color="#D900D9">(BEEPS)</font>

27
00:04:41.148 --> 00:04:43.482
<font color="#D900D9">(PHONE RINGING)</font>

28
00:04:47.855 --> 00:04:50.758
<i><font color="#808080">WOMAN:</font> How many times
have I told you not to call me here?</i>

29
00:04:50.858 --> 00:04:52.259
<font color="#D900D9">(BEEPS)</font>

30
00:04:52.559 --> 00:04:55.838
<i><font color="#808080">BEN:</font> Hey, it's me.</i>

31
00:04:56.663 --> 00:05:00.164
<i>Look, I know I forgot to say
that I love you.</i>

32
00:05:03.136 --> 00:05:07.705
<i>Well, I guess I just wanted
to hear your voice, so...</i>

33
00:05:09.176 --> 00:05:11.141
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

34
00:05:32.099 --> 00:05:34.320
<font color="#D900D9">(RAILROAD WARNING BELL DINGING)</font>

35
00:05:49.416 --> 00:05:51.184
<font color="#808080">MAN:</font> So you working through dinner?

36
00:05:51.284 --> 00:05:53.518
- <font color="#D900D9">(DOOR CLOSES)</font>
- Uh...

37
00:05:55.456 --> 00:05:57.224
<font color="#D900D9">(SIGHS)</font>

38
00:05:57.324 --> 00:06:00.858
Well, pick me
a good fortune cookie, huh?

39
00:06:01.922 --> 00:06:05.876
Yang's still doing the negotiations?
All right, okay.

40
00:06:07.301 --> 00:06:10.270
How many points you got left? Still six?

41
00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:13.507
- <font color="#D900D9">(KNOCKS)</font>
- Morning, Sheriff.

42
00:06:13.807 --> 00:06:15.309
Ready to earn?

43
00:06:15.409 --> 00:06:17.144
Yeah, black-tail or bear?

44
00:06:17.760 --> 00:06:20.814
- Bighorn.
- Little early in the season, isn't it?

45
00:06:20.914 --> 00:06:25.452
Seems he got himself a special exemption.
Got connections, I reckon.

46
00:06:25.552 --> 00:06:27.955
- Some kind of big shot.
- Yeah.

47
00:06:28.055 --> 00:06:32.526
He's paying a grand per day. Kind of
makes you overlook the little things.

48
00:06:32.626 --> 00:06:36.094
You got some crazy-ass dog problems
around here, huh?

49
00:06:37.731 --> 00:06:40.200
The problem is coyotes.
They like the taste.

50
00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:43.000
Yeah, yeah, no, we got
the same thing in LA, you know.

51
00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:44.519
One of them would come down
from the hills,

52
00:06:44.619 --> 00:06:47.576
starts flirting with some
old lady's shih tzu, and...

53
00:06:47.676 --> 00:06:51.910
lures it back up the hill
and bye-bye, shih tzu.

54
00:06:56.249 --> 00:06:59.350
- He's it?
- He's it.

55
00:07:00.654 --> 00:07:01.889
How old are you?

56
00:07:01.989 --> 00:07:05.226
Old enough to be the best tracker
in the county, if not the state.

57
00:07:05.355 --> 00:07:09.196
- Not quite, but I can get 'er done.
- Well, imagine that.

58
00:07:09.296 --> 00:07:13.311
You know, I pull off 85 thinking I found
a good place to take a dump. <font color="#D900D9">(LAUGHING)</font>

59
00:07:16.102 --> 00:07:17.702
Hey, John Madec.

60
00:07:18.972 --> 00:07:20.707
Ben.

61
00:07:20.807 --> 00:07:23.209
Ben. Okay.

62
00:07:23.309 --> 00:07:25.378
Just Ben. Let's roll, huh?

63
00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:29.483
Wait a second. I need to see
a driver's license and harvest permit.

64
00:07:30.083 --> 00:07:33.019
Uh, I took care of it.

65
00:07:33.119 --> 00:07:34.721
He's good to go, Deputy.

66
00:07:34.821 --> 00:07:37.622
Come on, we'll take my ride.
Sheriff, thank you.

67
00:07:45.699 --> 00:07:48.268
Only one in America.

68
00:07:48.368 --> 00:07:51.872
500K. That's not including tax.

69
00:07:51.972 --> 00:07:53.474
Uh-huh.

70
00:07:53.574 --> 00:07:56.479
- Well, I guess it doesn't park itself.
- <font color="#D900D9">(SCOFFS)</font>

71
00:07:57.333 --> 00:07:59.778
- Mind if I check your rifle?
- No, no. Sure. Here.

72
00:08:05.085 --> 00:08:09.089
Steyr Scout 308.
Had it imported from Austria.

73
00:08:09.189 --> 00:08:13.094
It's got a Leupold scope.
Best glass you can get out of Sweden.

74
00:08:13.994 --> 00:08:16.063
I've never seen one of these.

75
00:08:16.163 --> 00:08:19.965
Most folks around here use Brownings,
Winchesters, Remingtons.

76
00:08:25.605 --> 00:08:27.149
<font color="#D900D9">(ENGINE STARTS)</font>

77
00:08:51.465 --> 00:08:53.632
Mind if I take a look?

78
00:08:56.970 --> 00:08:59.206
- So what's her name?
- Laina.

79
00:08:59.306 --> 00:09:03.941
A real photograph.
Not one of those iPhones. Old school.

80
00:09:04.644 --> 00:09:06.179
She's lovely.

81
00:09:06.279 --> 00:09:11.084
Boy, a girl like that staying with you
in a place like this? You're a lucky guy.

82
00:09:11.184 --> 00:09:13.887
Actually, she's in school up in Denver.

83
00:09:13.987 --> 00:09:16.657
Oh, yeah? She's got some wits
in her, too, huh?

84
00:09:16.757 --> 00:09:18.723
Full ride. Swim team.

85
00:09:50.423 --> 00:09:52.056
<font color="#D900D9">(SQUEAKING)</font>

86
00:10:21.521 --> 00:10:24.289
Well, it seems like WALL-E
is definitely stuck here.

87
00:10:28.562 --> 00:10:30.604
WALL-E.

88
00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:39.580
WALL-E.

89
00:10:46.513 --> 00:10:49.347
WALL-E.

90
00:10:54.120 --> 00:10:56.715
- EVA.
- <font color="#D900D9">(LAUGHS)</font>

91
00:10:58.726 --> 00:11:02.312
Yeah, I knew I'd get a smile out of you.

92
00:11:12.338 --> 00:11:14.171
<font color="#808080">JOHN:</font> Hey.

93
00:11:15.642 --> 00:11:20.617
Beyond this point,
there will be monsters.

94
00:11:28.255 --> 00:11:31.856
Well, I suppose this is
where you earn your money.

95
00:11:44.471 --> 00:11:46.264
<font color="#D900D9">(PHONE RINGS)</font>

96
00:11:47.240 --> 00:11:49.476
There's no reception out here.

97
00:11:49.876 --> 00:11:53.413
It's a sat-phone.
Full terrestrial coverage.

98
00:11:53.513 --> 00:11:56.147
<font color="#D900D9">(SPEAKING CHINESE)</font>

99
00:11:58.551 --> 00:12:02.823
No, that's right. 8:00 AM tomorrow.
Midnight Beijing time.

100
00:12:02.923 --> 00:12:04.958
We'll try to wrap it all up.

101
00:12:05.258 --> 00:12:08.528
If they complain,
just tell them Confucius says,

102
00:12:08.628 --> 00:12:12.499
"Reset your fiscal year at one."

103
00:12:12.599 --> 00:12:14.365
Some shit like that. I don't know.

104
00:12:15.502 --> 00:12:17.738
<font color="#D900D9">(SPEAKS CHINESE)</font>

105
00:12:18.575 --> 00:12:19.806
Big deal?

106
00:12:19.906 --> 00:12:21.975
Uh, yeah, you could say that, yeah.

107
00:12:22.075 --> 00:12:24.577
So you in finance or something?

108
00:12:25.021 --> 00:12:27.480
- Insurance.
- What do you insure?

109
00:12:27.880 --> 00:12:29.957
Finance.

110
00:13:02.448 --> 00:13:05.018
300 million years ago,
all this was underwater,

111
00:13:05.938 --> 00:13:08.986
submerged in an inland sea.

112
00:13:13.893 --> 00:13:16.463
Well, I'm afraid I'm gonna have
to add to the erosion.

113
00:13:16.563 --> 00:13:18.062
<font color="#D900D9">(CHUCKLES)</font>

114
00:13:21.601 --> 00:13:23.303
<font color="#D900D9">(URINATING, SIGHS)</font>

115
00:13:23.403 --> 00:13:25.472
<font color="#D900D9">(ZIPPER UNZIPS)</font>

116
00:13:25.572 --> 00:13:28.072
<font color="#D900D9">(URINATING)</font>

117
00:13:30.076 --> 00:13:32.082
<font color="#D900D9">(SHEEP BELLOWING)</font>

118
00:13:38.351 --> 00:13:40.380
<font color="#D900D9">(LOUD CLACKING)</font>

119
00:13:41.754 --> 00:13:43.056
<font color="#808080">BEN:</font> There's your bighorn.

120
00:13:43.156 --> 00:13:45.192
<font color="#D900D9">(CHUCKLES)</font>

121
00:13:45.892 --> 00:13:49.893
Establishing a dominance hierarchy.

122
00:13:50.864 --> 00:13:53.400
It's weird. They don't usually
go at it this late.

123
00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:57.168
Women, they're good at getting your ire up
when all you want to do is sleep.

124
00:14:02.208 --> 00:14:03.374
Ah.

125
00:14:05.778 --> 00:14:07.681
<font color="#D900D9">(COYOTES HOWLING)</font>

126
00:14:07.881 --> 00:14:09.883
<font color="#D900D9">(SIGHS)</font>

127
00:14:10.383 --> 00:14:13.019
A lot of smart guys
in college, you know.

128
00:14:13.119 --> 00:14:16.022
Smart guys who get
turned on by smart girls.

129
00:14:16.322 --> 00:14:19.392
- You're not worried about that?
- Nope.

130
00:14:19.792 --> 00:14:22.166
'Cause it's true love?

131
00:14:22.266 --> 00:14:25.498
- We grew up together.
- Oh, so there's no mystery.

132
00:14:25.698 --> 00:14:27.000
Exactly.

133
00:14:27.904 --> 00:14:29.033
<font color="#D900D9">(CHUCKLES)</font> Exactly.

134
00:14:30.803 --> 00:14:33.757
- <font color="#D900D9">(BEEPING)</font>
- What was that?

135
00:14:33.857 --> 00:14:36.707
That is a civilized man's dinner.

136
00:14:40.346 --> 00:14:43.516
Well, you know, I suppose
you couldn't go with her.

137
00:14:43.616 --> 00:14:48.588
But with all the glorious opportunities
that you have in this fine place...

138
00:14:48.988 --> 00:14:50.655
It's a family business.

139
00:14:52.792 --> 00:14:55.996
My parents were guides.
Search and Rescue for 20 years.

140
00:14:56.096 --> 00:14:59.163
Yeah, until they came to their senses.

141
00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:09.073
They died, right?

142
00:15:15.515 --> 00:15:17.650
The sheriff called you deputy.

143
00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:19.819
That makes the S&R paperwork easier.

144
00:15:20.548 --> 00:15:24.287
Search and Rescue, huh?
You get that much action out here?

145
00:15:25.358 --> 00:15:27.327
There was a pileup on the highway.

146
00:15:27.427 --> 00:15:31.295
So this old station wagon
tried to find a way around.

147
00:15:32.165 --> 00:15:34.467
When the thing stalled,

148
00:15:34.567 --> 00:15:36.701
they just left it.

149
00:15:36.801 --> 00:15:38.538
A family of four.

150
00:15:38.838 --> 00:15:41.041
And the thing is, they weren't
even a mile from the highway.

151
00:15:41.141 --> 00:15:42.876
Of course they couldn't see it
'cause of the ridge

152
00:15:42.976 --> 00:15:47.414
or hear it 'cause it was still
clogged up. So they guessed.

153
00:15:47.914 --> 00:15:51.181
Just headed out across the reach.

154
00:15:51.985 --> 00:15:53.486
Well, they didn't get far.

155
00:15:53.586 --> 00:15:56.623
It only takes a few hours
exposed like that.

156
00:15:56.723 --> 00:15:59.326
The dad was about a mile from the car.

157
00:16:00.426 --> 00:16:02.226
The mom, she had...

158
00:16:06.066 --> 00:16:10.735
she had smeared lipstick on her kids' faces
to try to stop the burning.

159
00:16:16.409 --> 00:16:19.629
Well, you know,
at least they put up a fight.

160
00:16:19.879 --> 00:16:20.981
They killed themselves.

161
00:16:21.081 --> 00:16:25.149
They took a chance,
they made their stand. I mean...

162
00:16:35.461 --> 00:16:37.428
<font color="#D900D9">(OWL HOOTING)</font>

163
00:16:55.815 --> 00:16:57.548
Oh, my God.

164
00:17:01.888 --> 00:17:03.439
Come with me, Ben.

165
00:17:03.539 --> 00:17:05.623
<font color="#D900D9">(COFFEEMAKER HISSING)</font>

166
00:17:16.903 --> 00:17:18.505
You want a single or a double?

167
00:17:19.249 --> 00:17:20.807
What?

168
00:17:21.507 --> 00:17:23.143
Single or a double?

169
00:17:24.229 --> 00:17:26.125
No.

170
00:17:30.416 --> 00:17:32.450
<font color="#D900D9">(SIGHS)</font>

171
00:17:33.753 --> 00:17:36.201
Let's go, Ben.

172
00:17:36.923 --> 00:17:39.006
<font color="#D900D9">(BIRD SCREECHING)</font>

173
00:17:58.444 --> 00:18:01.247
It's a local shooting gallery.

174
00:18:01.347 --> 00:18:02.813
<font color="#D900D9">(COCKS GUN)</font>

175
00:18:09.122 --> 00:18:10.766
<font color="#D900D9">(GUNSHOTS ECHOING)</font>

176
00:18:17.029 --> 00:18:19.432
- What are you doing?
- I'm just warming up.

177
00:18:19.532 --> 00:18:21.732
When you fire your weapon,
you frighten the game.

178
00:18:23.670 --> 00:18:26.904
They're already frightened.
That's why they're being hunted.

179
00:18:33.579 --> 00:18:35.946
- You forgetting something?
- Hmm?

180
00:18:37.550 --> 00:18:39.385
Your brass.

181
00:18:39.485 --> 00:18:42.019
That's your job.

182
00:19:02.675 --> 00:19:04.777
You been hunting long?

183
00:19:04.877 --> 00:19:08.248
Probably before you were
wearing Huggies, kid.

184
00:19:08.648 --> 00:19:10.917
Your Steyr looks brand-new.

185
00:19:11.017 --> 00:19:14.087
Well, I take care of my equipment.

186
00:19:14.187 --> 00:19:16.354
Sounds like you have other people do it.

187
00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:20.960
I'm no amateur, okay, kid?

188
00:19:21.060 --> 00:19:23.729
I mean, I've got the horns to prove it.

189
00:19:23.829 --> 00:19:27.064
Rhino, elephant.

190
00:19:29.402 --> 00:19:31.691
Trophies, huh? <font color="#D900D9">(SNIFFS)</font>

191
00:19:33.472 --> 00:19:34.874
So that's your thing?

192
00:19:34.974 --> 00:19:37.810
Well, it sure isn't
for the company or the frills.

193
00:19:38.838 --> 00:19:42.445
There ain't no greater exercise
in boredom.

194
00:19:42.949 --> 00:19:44.084
But you're right. I, uh...

195
00:19:44.184 --> 00:19:47.253
I bought this baby special
when I landed my bighorn permit.

196
00:19:47.553 --> 00:19:50.523
Been waiting to fill
that last little space on the wall.

197
00:19:50.623 --> 00:19:54.558
- You get a gender exemption?
- Yeah, dulled male only.

198
00:19:57.063 --> 00:19:59.363
You mind if I just double-check
that permit?

199
00:20:07.807 --> 00:20:10.843
You know what the odds are
for landing a bighorn license?

200
00:20:11.653 --> 00:20:13.246
I sure do.

201
00:20:13.546 --> 00:20:15.481
10 years.

202
00:20:15.581 --> 00:20:17.815
10 years I've been trying to get one.

203
00:20:42.875 --> 00:20:45.776
That seemed to satisfy your sheriff.

204
00:20:52.952 --> 00:20:56.525
No, no, right.
You know, it's more time and...

205
00:20:56.865 --> 00:21:00.457
you got your family business
to maintain.

206
00:21:01.561 --> 00:21:02.993
A tough economy.

207
00:21:27.186 --> 00:21:30.921
All right, just Ben. Meter's running.

208
00:21:58.584 --> 00:22:01.151
<font color="#808080">JOHN:</font> You see anything?

209
00:22:03.623 --> 00:22:05.992
Best tracker in the county, huh?

210
00:22:06.092 --> 00:22:10.260
Well, the job is easier if you're quiet.

211
00:22:20.006 --> 00:22:21.340
<font color="#D900D9">(ROCKS FALLING)</font>

212
00:22:23.275 --> 00:22:25.209
<font color="#D900D9">(GUNSHOT ECHOES)</font>

213
00:22:29.682 --> 00:22:33.017
This may have been the easiest money
you ever made, buddy.

214
00:22:52.138 --> 00:22:53.973
<font color="#D900D9">(FLIES BUZZING)</font>

215
00:22:54.073 --> 00:22:56.542
No! Oh, my God.

216
00:22:56.642 --> 00:23:00.663
Jesus Christ, no! No.

217
00:23:01.167 --> 00:23:04.214
- Charlie.
- God damn it.

218
00:23:06.385 --> 00:23:09.787
Where'd he come from? Jesus Christ.

219
00:23:10.956 --> 00:23:15.159
God Almighty. Oh, Christ.

220
00:23:21.434 --> 00:23:23.470
Is he dead?

221
00:23:24.170 --> 00:23:26.303
Oh, God Almighty.

222
00:23:29.942 --> 00:23:33.444
- Did you know him?
- Yeah, my whole life.

223
00:23:35.014 --> 00:23:37.416
Okay. Okay.

224
00:23:37.516 --> 00:23:39.452
- We need to take him to town.
- What?

225
00:23:39.852 --> 00:23:43.389
- We need to take him to town, all right?
- All right, here.

226
00:23:43.489 --> 00:23:46.192
All right, I'll... I'll stay with him.

227
00:23:46.292 --> 00:23:48.728
- Jesus.
- All right.

228
00:23:48.828 --> 00:23:51.462
- Stay there.
- Oh, Jesus Christ.

229
00:23:54.800 --> 00:23:56.834
Shit.

230
00:24:26.732 --> 00:24:28.098
<font color="#D900D9">(DIALING)</font>

231
00:24:31.036 --> 00:24:32.621
Hey,

232
00:24:32.721 --> 00:24:35.676
listen, I'm in a shitstorm here, all right?
It might jeopardize the deal,

233
00:24:35.776 --> 00:24:38.808
so listen up.

234
00:24:49.555 --> 00:24:53.757
I pay you for options, all right?
So give me one!

235
